# 1. 8-rectangle (rows 1-4, cols 1-7): borders stay as 8, interior (rows 2-3, cols 2-6) 
#    gets checkerboard fill of 3 where (r+c)%2==0
# 2. 4-rectangle (rows 6-13, cols 12-18): borders as 4, interior gets complex 6-pattern
#    Pattern seems to be: every row has 6s at cols where (c - some_offset) % 2 == 1
#    Looking at the output more carefully...

# Actually let me just implement based on observed pattern and test

